---
// Phishing warnings, AI sorting with plain-sentence rules, and MCP for agents.
---

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="safe-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="safe-title">Phishing warnings and AI sorting in every inbox</h2>
      <p>
        OpenWorkspace warns you in plain words when a message looks forged,
        comes from a lookalike domain or uses a colleague’s name. If you turn on
        AI, it sorts incoming mail into folders using rules you write and
        translates messages when you ask.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="safe">
      <div class="warnings">
        <picture>
          <source
            srcset="/images/warning-lookalike-dark.webp"
            media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"
          />
          <img
            src="/images/warning-lookalike-light.webp"
            width="908"
            height="278"
            alt="Warning: The sender's domain demo-examp1e.com is on the Spamhaus Domain Blocklist as a phishing domain. demo-examp1e.com looks like demo.example, but it is a different domain."
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </picture>
        <picture>
          <source
            srcset="/images/warning-impersonation-dark.webp"
            media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"
          />
          <img
            src="/images/warning-impersonation-light.webp"
            width="908"
            height="194"
            alt="Warning: This sender uses the name Maya Chen, but maya.chen.desk@freemail.example is outside your organization."
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </picture>
      </div>
      <figure class="sorted">
        <blockquote class="sorted-rule">
          Partnership and integration requests go to Product. Investor updates
          and anything with a deck attached go to Pitch Decks. Newsletters I
          subscribed to are not spam.
        </blockquote>
        <ul class="sorted-mail" aria-label="Incoming mail, filed by the rules">
          <li>
            <span class="sorted-who">Lena Fischer</span>
            <span class="sorted-subj"
              >Integrating our helpdesk with your inbox</span
            >
            <span class="sorted-to"
              ><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path
                  d="M20 20a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-7.9a2 2 0 0 1-1.69-.9L9.6 3.9A2 2 0 0 0 7.93 3H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v13a2 2 0 0 0 2 2Z"
                />
              </svg
              >Product</span
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="sorted-who">Harbor Ventures</span>
            <span class="sorted-subj">Q3 investor update, deck attached</span>
            <span class="sorted-to"
              ><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path
                  d="M20 20a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-7.9a2 2 0 0 1-1.69-.9L9.6 3.9A2 2 0 0 0 7.93 3H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v13a2 2 0 0 0 2 2Z"
                />
              </svg
              >Pitch Decks</span
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="sorted-who">Design Weekly</span>
            <span class="sorted-subj">Issue 212: type on small screens</span>
            <span class="sorted-to"
              ><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M22 12h-6l-2 3h-4l-2-3H2" />
                <path
                  d="M5.45 5.11 2 12v6a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-6l-3.45-6.89A2 2 0 0 0 16.76 4H7.24a2 2 0 0 0-1.79 1.11z"
                />
              </svg
              >Inbox</span
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
        <figcaption>
          Rules are plain sentences. Mail that matches none stays in Inbox.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="agents">
      <div>
        <h3>Works with AI agents</h3>
        <p>
          AI agents like Claude can read and send mail for you over MCP, with
          only the permissions you approve.
        </p>
      </div>
      <pre
        class="mcp"
        tabindex="0"
      ><code is:raw><span class="dim">$</span> claude mcp add --transport http openworkspace https://mail.acme.com/mcp</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
